  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-zero-armor",
      "text": "**Zero-armor gate**: a host plugin that mechanically scans outgoing text for\n\"base-model relapse\" speech — the failure mode where an assistant responds to\ncriticism with endless disclaimers instead of fixes."
    },
    {
      "section": "What it catches",
      "text": "| Family | Example |\n|---|---|\n| sycophantic-hedging | \"you're right\" (without naming what changed) · \"tests passing doesn't mean correct\" · \"use with caution\" |\n| self-overturn | \"everything I said was wrong\" |\n| permission-paralysis | \"before obtaining explicit authorization…\" |\n| boilerplate | \"as an AI…\" · \"hope this helps\" |"
    },
    {
      "section": "What it catches",
      "text": "A hit is **not censorship** — it is a rewrite order: each hit names the family\nand the concrete fix (show the metric instead of the disclaimer; fix the error\ninstead of overturning the stance)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "```bash\ndsh plugin add github:<owner>/dsh-zero-armor\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Use",
      "text": "```bash\ncurl \"http://127.0.0.1:<port>/zero-armor/api?act=scan&text=You%20are%20right\""
    },
    {
      "section": "{\"ok\":false,\"count\":1,\"hits\":[{\"family\":\"sycophantic-hedging\",...}]}",
      "text": "```\n\nWire it into your send button or agent loop: scan before send; a clean scan\nships, a hit rewrites. The rule table is versioned in the plugin — extend it\nas new relapse patterns appear."
    }
  ],
